# Face API conventions

## Stack

- Embeddings: InsightFace `buffalo_l`, `vector(512)` in `face_encoding`
- Devices: prefer **one visible GPU per API process** (`CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` + `FACE_DEVICES=cuda:0`). Dual-GPU host → `api` + `api-gpu1` via `docker-compose.gpu.yml`
- `get_face_app` must pass ORT `provider_options=[{"device_id": N}, {}]` — `prepare(ctx_id=N)` alone can leave both sessions on GPU0
- In-process queue: **all** InsightFace inference (`generate_face_encoding`, `verify_liveness_and_get_encoding`, `extract_face_features*`, `detect_faces*`) must run via `run_on_face_gpu`; JPEG decode uses a **separate** ThreadPoolExecutor (`get_decode_executor`)
- Detect-only path uses `FACE_DETECT_DET_SIZE` (320); embedding uses `FACE_EMBED_DET_SIZE` (640)
- Threshold: `FACE_RECOGNITION_THRESHOLD` (cosine distance; match if `< threshold`)
- 1:N match lives in `services/face_match_service.py` (`SET LOCAL hnsw.ef_search` + JOIN `company_employee` + JOIN `member` filtering `deletedAt IS NULL` and `Member.status == ENABLE`)

## Auth & Multi-Tenancy

- `FACE_ROUTES_REQUIRE_JWT=true` by default. HTTP routes get the member from `AuthzMiddleware`; form `companyId` is bound with `assert_request_company_access`; `memberId` / `faceEncodingId` routes use `assert_member_company_access` / `assert_encoding_company_access`
- WS `/face/ws/kiosk`: `session` message must include `token`; company access is checked before frames are accepted, and `token_exp` is enforced on every frame
- WS `detect` returns `dropped: true` when the queue passes `WS_QUEUE_BACKPRESSURE` or per-connection `task_sem` (`Semaphore(4)`) is full

## Endpoints (do not regress)

| Path | Mode |
|------|------|
| `POST /face/members/{id}/add-face` | enroll (via `run_on_face_gpu`) |
| `POST /face/members/check-face-emp` | multi-frame + liveness match (**companyId** required, via `run_on_face_gpu`) |
| `POST /face/members/identify` | 1 frame, label only (**companyId** required) |
| `POST /face/members/check-in` | secure: liveness + timestamp (optional `punchType`: `AUTO` \| `CHECK_IN` \| `CHECK_OUT`) |
| `POST /face/members/check-in-walkby` | 1–3 frames, no motion liveness (optional `punchType`: `AUTO` \| `CHECK_IN` \| `CHECK_OUT`) |
| `WS /face/ws/kiosk` | stream identify/checkin via GPU queue (supports `punchType`) |
| `GET /face/queue-stats` | queue health |

Shared finalize: `_finalize_check_in` (match **within company** → active company employee → dedupe (with explicit mode bypass) → photo → hybrid `create_timestamp` with shift Late/OT).

## Rules

- Face 1:N search must be company-scoped (`companyId`) and active-employee-scoped — never match across companies or against soft-deleted/disabled members
- Prefer extending `face_controller` / `face_engine` / `face_gpu_queue` over new parallel pipelines
- Dedupe: `CHECK_IN_DEDUPE_SECONDS` (default 300) — return `duplicate: true` in `AUTO` mode; allow explicit `CHECK_OUT` after recent `CHECK_IN` (`_should_bypass_dedupe_for_explicit_mode`)
- Outside geofence: `create_timestamp` needs a `note` — kiosk sends a default note
- Do not add `DROP TABLE` or `create_all`-style destructive steps at startup; schema changes go in `utils/schema_migrate.py` (idempotent SQL) and an Alembic revision under `API-Fast/alembic/versions/`
- Mutating handlers are audited by the middleware; do not log passwords, tokens, or embeddings
